rd (22,179 postings) and Meta; the first-page preview on Amazon (real cards under "Loading 22,179 roles…", then the list replaces them); Google's job-family departments with the Company group-by and filter; the one-line notes with one Details disclosure (fix-density); "· 2 levels" and "· N places" cards, "from €X" minimums and shift-pay labels; the clusters chart, whose circles now sit at their postings' median pay, and the Ranges view, where identical posted bands are stacked into one row with ×N (viz-even). Also re-check that earlier findings stay fixed. Known open items you need not re-report, but may add evidence to: MR-23 (FX rates from 2026-07-01, waiting on the user), MR-26, MR-28, MR-29 (the on-screen label), MR-33 to MR-35, MR-37 to MR-42 in docs/process/methodology-review-beta-2.md, and the Insights tab on Amazon being one 4.3 s task (docs/process/perf-mobile-beta-2.md). The text-density check is a hard check: measure every secondary line on 390x844 and 360x740. You work in your own worktree, so do NOT edit docs/QA.md (another QA agent writes the same file at the same time): put your whole QA section, in docs/QA.md's format, at the end of your own log docs/process/qa-mobile-beta-3.md under a heading "## Section for docs/QA.md", and the lead copies it in when integrating.
